_at":"2025-03-27T16:31:31Z","body":"> I noticed there's code for\n> \n> [godot/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/594d64ec244b6b99321e2096987d4d69de4c8845/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp#L802)\n> \n> Line 802 in [594d64e](/godotengine/godot/commit/594d64ec244b6b99321e2096987d4d69de4c8845)\n>  #ifdef REAL_T_IS_DOUBLE \n> \n> here but no code for the instanced transforms.\n> \n> [godot/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/594d64ec244b6b99321e2096987d4d69de4c8845/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp#L4218)\n> \n> Line 4218 in [594d64e](/godotengine/godot/commit/594d64ec244b6b99321e2096987d4d69de4c8845)\n>  ginstance->transforms_uniform_set = mesh_storage->multimesh_get_3d_uniform_set(ginstance->data->base, scene_shader.default_shader_rd, TRANSFORMS_UNIFORM_SET); \n> \n> Are you able to look into these clues and patch it? I'm still working on our social vr project and inverse kinematics. I suspect clayjohn is busy.\n\nI followed this path for a bit last night, but didn't see anything suspicious. The `#ifdef REAL_T_IS_DOUBLE` on line 802 is splitting the origin up, but I don't believe that would cause incorrect rotation further down the line. And I haven't noticed any precision issues with multimesh, just rotation. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2758668975/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2758894073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104654#issuecomment-2758894073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godote